{
  "topic": "chernobyl",
  "ttsScript": "Reactor Four surged to thirty thousand megawatts in four seconds. One hundred times its safe limit. Everyone blamed the operators. Reckless. Incompetent. But the operators were following direct orders from their supervisor, Dyatlov. The real killer was the RBMK reactor itself. Its control rods had graphite tips. Pushing them in caused a power spike instead of stopping it. The Soviet government knew about this flaw for years. They classified the report and told no one. The coverup killed more people than the explosion ever did.",
